# Basebase Framework - AI Assistant Rules

## CRITICAL: DO NOT EDIT FRAMEWORK CODE

**ONLY modify files in the `/app` directory.**

### ✅ You CAN edit:
- `app/**/*` - All application code
- `app/components/**` - React components
- `app/stores/**` - Zustand stores
- `app/schema.js` - Data structure definitions
- `app/app.jsx` - Main entry point

### ❌ NEVER edit:
- `framework/**/*` - Core framework code
- `scripts/**/*` - Build/deployment scripts
- `vite.config.js` - Build configuration
- `package.json` - Dependencies (unless adding new app dependencies)

### Why?
- Framework code is shared across all apps
- Only `/app` folder contents are committed to Firestore
- Changes outside `/app` will work locally but FAIL in production
- Framework updates are managed by the platform team

### Workflow:
1. User creates/edits files in `/app` folder ONLY
2. Test locally with `npm run dev`
3. Commit with `npm run app:commit <appId>`
4. Only `/app` folder contents are uploaded to Firestore

**If you're asked to modify anything outside `/app`, politely decline and explain this restriction.**

